AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75832> "A compound of iron and sulfate in which the ratio of iron(2+) to sulfate ions is 1:1. Various hydrates occur naturally - most commonly the heptahydrate, which loses water to form the tetrahydrate at 57degreeC and the monohydrate at 65degreeC.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75832> "iron(2+) sulfate (anhydrous)")
