# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411236> (turkey (bird))

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411236> "The turkey is a large bird in the genus Meleagris, which is native to the Americas. Males of both turkey species have a distinctive fleshy wattle or protuberance that hangs from the top of the beak (called a snood). They are among the largest birds in their ranges. As in many galliformes, the male is larger and much more colorful than the female."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411236> <http://eol.org/pages/18523>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411236> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=B1236>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411236> "turkey (bird)"@en)
