# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420228> (extract, concentrate or isolate of plant or animal)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420228> "A physical-chemical component separated from the food source or its parts by extraction, centrifugation, filtration, heat processing, expressing or a similar process. The separated component may be converted through further processing. If this is done, the final substance is indexed. A water-extracted component may remain in aqueous dispersion. The extract, concentrate or isolate is indexed in preference to the anatomic part from which it is derived. For example, peanut oil is indexed under *PEANUT* combined wih *FAT OR OIL* rather than with *SEED OR KERNEL*. On the other hand, fruit and vegetable juices can be indexed under *FRUIT JUICE OR NECTAR* or *VEGETABLE JUICE* (A. PRODUCT TYPE); therefore the anatomic part of the plant should be indexed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420228> "langual:C0228")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420228> "Damion Dooley's note: Items in this branch will be merged into foodon food product branch."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420228> "extract, concentrate or isolate of plant or animal"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420228> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001714>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420229> (fruit, peel removed, core, pit or seed removed)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420229> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=C0229>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420229> "LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *FRUIT OR BERRY, PEEL REMOVED, CORE, PIT OR SEED REMOVED* in LanguaL 2008."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420229> "fruit, peel removed, core, pit or seed removed"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420229> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420138>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420238> (root, tuber or bulb)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420238> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=C0238>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420238> "root, tuber or bulb"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420238> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420148>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420245> (mammalian milk curd)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420245> "The thicker or more coagulable part of milk that is separated from the serum or watery part (whey), especially in the process of making cheese."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420245> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=C0245>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420245> "curd"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420245> "mammalian milk curd"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420245> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03315150>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420288> (seed bran)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420288> "The broken outer coat, or husk, of grains of wheat, rye, oats, etc. separated from the flour after grinding, as by sifting (Source: Webster's)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420288> "LANGUAL:C0288"^^rdfs:Literal)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420288> "seed bran"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420288> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420178>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420307> (seed oil)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420307> "The oil produced by pressing or extracting lipids from plant seeds (e.g. grapeseed oil, rapeseed oil, linseed oil) /AM"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420307> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=C0307>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420307> "seed oil"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420307> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001087>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430106> (finely ground)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430106> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=E0106>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430106> "finely ground"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430106> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430136>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113> (food physical quality)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113> "The physical state of the food product (liquid, semiliquid, semisolid, or solid). Solid food products are further subdivided by shape or form. Terms are provided for products that have both liquid and solid components or that incorporate air or other gases. [FDA CFSAN 1995]"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=E0113>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113> "Damion Dooley's note: these categories need to be mapped over to PATO phenotypic categories, with a suitable treatment of mixtures of solids that are divided into parts."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113> "food physical quality"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002470>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> (divided or disintegrated)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=E0122>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> "LanguaL curation note: The distinctions in this category are based on size characteristics, primarily thickness, which are important for heat transfer and for diffusion of chemicals in processing. *DIVIDED INTO HALVES, QUARTERS OR SEGMENTS* should be examined first and if one of the descriptors listed applies it should be used regardless of the size of the pieces. If none of these are applicable, other *DIVIDED OR DISINTEGRATED* descriptors should be examined. Do not use any of these descriptors if dividing or disintegrating results in a semiliquid or semisolid product."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> "divided or disintegrated"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430113>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> (food (liquid))

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> "A state of matter between a solid and a gas, in which a substance has the capacity to flow and conforms to the shape of the container."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=E0130>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> <https://bioregistry.io/reference/siren:F5105>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> "Liquids range from water to honey, corresponding to a range in viscosity (or apparent viscosity) from 1 to 500 centipoise (viscosity is a measure of a liquid's resistance to flow). Products that are pourable but have a higher viscosity are *SEMILIQUID*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> "food (liquid)"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> ObjectIntersectionOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002454> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001548>)))
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002454>)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430130> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001548>))

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430136> (disintegrated or ground)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430136> <http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=E0136>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430136> "LanguaL curation note: Used when particle size is below 0.2 cm."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430136> "disintegrated or ground"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430122>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450002> (food cooking)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450002> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=G0002")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450002> "food cooking"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450002> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004> (cooking by dry heat)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004> "Cooked at moderate to high levels of heat in which no liquid is added and only small amounts of fat may be added to prevent sticking."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=G0004")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004> "LanguaL"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004> "cooking by dry heat"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450002>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450005> (food baking)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450005> "Cooked without moisture, covered or uncovered, in an oven."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450005> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=G0005")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450005> "food baking"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450005> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450004>)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03450005> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002456>))

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111> (food treatment process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111> "Used to specifically characterize a food product based on the treatment or processes applied to the product or any indexed ingredient. The processes include adding, substituting or removing components or modifying the food or component, e.g., through fermentation."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0111")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111> "LanguaL curation note: This term is for CLASSIFICATION ONLY; DO NOT USE term in indexing. Use a more precise narrower term."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111> "food treatment process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002451>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460119> (microbial/enzymatic modification process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460119> "A food modification process by microbial or enzymatic action which results in molecular changes in any food component."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460119> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0119")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460119> "LanguaL curation note: If salt, sugar or other food additive is used to aid in the modification process, index it by the appropriate term under *INGREDIENT ADDED*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460119> "microbial/enzymatic modification process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460130> (physical/chemical modification process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460130> "A food modification process where physical or chemical changes are effected in any food ingredient through a physical or non-enzymatic chemical process."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460130> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0130")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460130> "physical/chemical modification process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460130> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141> (food modification process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0141")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141> "LanguaL curation note: Used when the food product underwent mechanical, chemical or enzymatic modification that has affected the texture, flavor or other characteristic of the product."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141> "food modification process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460141> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460161> (fat removal process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460161> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0161")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460161> "LanguaL curation note: Used for products that contain less than 60% of the fat naturally present in the food source (more precisely, the part of the food source.) more specific fat levels, which vary from one product type to another, are specified in the extended scope notes for *FAT PARTIALLY REMOVED* and *FAT FULLY REMOVED* in the manual."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460161> "fat removal process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460161> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460177> (plant seed or nut food product)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460177> "langual:H0177")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460177> "LanguaL curation note: With the exception of peanut (see *PEANUT OR PEANUT BUTTER ADDED*), used when a nut or seed ingredient is the second ingredient in order of predominance."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460177> "plant seed or nut food product"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460177> ObjectUnionOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001172> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001173>))
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460177> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001015>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460207> (food filling process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460207> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0207")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460207> "LanguaL curation note: Applies to all filled or stuffed products, including pies and sandwiches."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460207> "food filling process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460207> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460130>)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460207> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000293> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001868>))

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460230> (single component food fermentation)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460230> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0230")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460230> "LanguaL curation note: Used for products in which either carbohydrates, proteins or fats were modified through microbial processes. Enzymatic or other biological processes may also be involved. If two or more of these components are modified in significant amounts, index under *FERMENTED/MODIFIED, MULTIPLE COMPONENT*."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460230> "single component food fermentation"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460230> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001304>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238> (food component separation process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238> "A component separation process at the very least removes one component from an initial entity.  The removed component may be captured as a process output for reuse if not destroyed in the process of removal."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0238")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238> "LanguaL curation note: Use the appropriate term under *COMPONENT REMOVED* to indicate the permanent full or partial removal of a nutritional/chemical component naturally present in the part of plant or animal used."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238> "food component separation process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460238> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460111>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460248> (full fat removal process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460248> "http://www.langual.org/langual_thesaurus.asp?termid=H0248")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460248> "LanguaL curation note: Used for products that contain less than 10-20% of the fat naturally present in the food source. Examples are skim milk, low-fat cocoa and dry-curd cottage cheese."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460248> "full fat removal process"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460248> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460161>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03460256> (carbohydrate fermentation)

